umo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" ti=
tle=3D""> and the <em>Site Identity</em> button <img alt=3D"Fx89Padlock" cl=
ass=3D"wiki-image frameless lazy" data-original-src=3D"https://assets-prod.=
sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/media/uploads/gallery/images/2021-05-06-04=
-33-33-7bdc86.png" src=3D"https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.=
net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965e3.gif" title=3D""></span><span class=
=3D"for" data-for=3D"fx149"> the <em>Tracking Protection</em> button <img a=
lt=3D"Fx149UnifiedTrustIcon-Secure" class=3D"wiki-image frameless lazy" dat=
a-original-src=3D"https://assets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/medi=
a/uploads/gallery/images/2026-01-28-01-16-02-8c168d.png" src=3D"https://ass=
ets-prod.sumo.prod.webservices.mozgcp.net/static/placeholder.cb78bf81388965=
e3.gif" title=3D""></span> in the pop-up window, the pop-up is coming from =
Firefox.
</li><li>If you don't see these buttons, you may have malware on your compu=
ter that causes the pop-ups. For help, see <a href=3D"https://support.mozil=
la.org/en-US/kb/troubleshoot-firefox-issues-caused-malware">Troubleshoot Fi=
refox issues caused by malware</a>.
</li></ul>
